A||||6||fogglethorpe||Twisted fairy tales||||5||
Z||000000||fogglethorpe||11-03-2001||01:24 PM||||Once upon a time, in a land that exists only in the minds of those who have bounced their reality checks,<BR>   there lived three little pigs, who, for sensitive reasons involving political correctness, shall henceforth be referred to as "Hammy Americans".<BR>   It seems our three little friends decided to build their dreamhome, and live in it together. Because of their reluctance to kill trees, and against the advice of their building contractor, they used environmentally friendly, cruelty-free building materials for said house, namely mud, popcorn, tree sap, clamshells, etc.<BR>   It turns out that the building inspector got wind of this, and paid our Hammy friends a visit.<BR>   The inspector was a big, bad wolf (henceforth referred to as a Canine-American with negatively impacted self-esteem, and anger management issues). He never liked Hammy-Americans anyway, and saw this as an opportunity to wreak some havoc upon them.<BR>   He arrived at their all natural abode, and proceeded to taunt them with vicious slurs, such as "mud-snorter" and "oinker", and even went so far as to suggest that their body parts would make good tavern food. Then he huffed, and puffed, and smashed their home to miniscule little bits with a wrecking ball.<BR>   The Hammy-Americans relocated to a local hotel, and secured legal counsel immediately.<BR>   They sued the daylights out of the Canine-American, citing vandalism and species-discrimination. The Canine-American had no choice but to plead guilty, and he was instructed by the judge to attend sensitivity training to deal with his anger, and disdain for the Hammy members of society. He was also prescribed Prozac, and made to pay back the Hammy-Americans for their home, and emotional trauma.<BR>   He is now on a national speaking tour, in support of his new book, "Huffing, Puffing, and Healing."<P><BR>..................<BR>intertwining fact & fiction,<BR>refining it to twisted diction<BR>     ||||reg||5
Z||000001||maryjane||11-03-2001||02:31 PM||||And the moral to this would be....?||||reg||1
