Z||000006||fogglethorpe||11-04-2001||04:11 PM|||| Since you have all been such good boys and girls, and<BR>didn't glue the parakeet to the cat's tail again, I will tell<BR>you another story:<BR>   Once upon a time, in a land that exists only in the minds<BR>of those who have bounced their reality checks,<BR>   there lived an environmental  scientist named Dr. Ducky Lucky.<BR>He and his assistant, Dr. Turkey Lurkey, worked tirelessly at<BR>Charlatan Labs, Inc., trying to spend their entire year's Government<BR>grant money proving that farts dissolve the ozone layer.<BR>   One day, as Dr. Lucky was on his way to purchase research<BR>materials such as beans, cabbage, and beer, he stepped outside<BR>the lab and was struck on the head by a white, sticky, globulus<BR>substance. Immediately, he ran back inside and emphatically<BR>announced to Dr. Lurkey, "The sky is falling, I tell you! A piece<BR>of it just hit me on the head!".<BR>   After showering, Dr. Lucky set out to reveal his alarming <BR>discovery to the rest of the world.<BR>   First, he wrote a book entitled, "There is stuff falling out of<BR>the sky, and I think it's the sky!". With the notoriety he gained<BR>from the book, he was featured on the cover of "Junk Science<BR>Monthly" magazine. He formed a PAC, and lobbied Congress<BR>to pass the "Flatulence Containment and Utilization Act", which<BR>would require public institutions such as restaurants to install<BR>Charlatan Labs'  "Smart-fart System" to protect the ozone,<BR> and conserve resources.<BR>   Dr. Ducky Lucky had become a household name, a revered<BR>scientific icon. And, because he had become wealthy and<BR> conceited as well, he considered Dr. Lurkey expendable, and<BR>fired him without warning or explanation.<BR>   The next day, the flabbergasted Dr. Lurkey cleared out his<BR>desk, and walked out of Charlatan Labs for good. Suddenly,<BR>the same white, gooey substance that had previously struck<BR>the cranium of his former boss struck him as well. He looked<BR>around, thought for a moment, and got a gloriously wicked<BR>idea. He would soon avenge his groundless dismissal, and<BR>be vindicated.<BR>   After showering, he too set out to reveal his discovery to <BR>the world. All he needed to do so was a Polaroid camera,<BR> with which he photographed the large robin's nest on the tree<BR>branch above Charlatan's front door. With the photos, it <BR>was easy to expose Dr. Ducky Lucky for the quack he was.<BR>   Soon, the only hot air people wanted to restrict was that<BR>which was spouted from Dr. Lucky's beak, and he was forced<BR>to flee to the South of France, to live in the wine country.<BR>   The brilliant Dr. Lurkey became rich and famous for <BR>marketing a paint remover made from bird droppings.<BR>||||reg||1
